 "doc": "I24 prereg sidecar (BUILD_PLAN I24 'Preregister': the basis count |E|-|V|+kappa computed in the prereg, each fixture's derived law and outcome, the new Morph laws beyond M0). Computed at the prereg by tests_m3/_i24x.py::par_basis_doc (rules X0-X9 and P0-P12 of the docstring of tests_m3/test_derive_par.py, written out a second time, independently of holon/) from the inputs listed with their sha256: the M3 adoption (spec/M3/lib/derive_extracted.json: the three extracted documents that replace the M0-M2 hand documents, Q19), the link roles (spec/M3/lib/link.json, I19's roles verbatim), the documents themselves and the I14 E6 lexicon. How each value was computed: (1) components: one per link role whose Solidity source is a loader edge and whose Go source is a tagged predicate (rule X1); for Morph the role header_length links the Solidity loader load_sol (input type Bytes) with the Go predicate (morph-l2/common/batch.BatchHeaderBytes).validate, so the component holds enc_sol and load_sol (morph_header.extracted.json), the encoders BatchHeaderV0.Bytes and BatchHeaderV1.Bytes, the patch (*BatchCache).createBatchHeaderWithSequencerSetHash, the 14 BatchHeaderBytes getters and validate (morph_batch.go.extracted.json). (2) carriers and functions: rules X2-X5 (names, layouts by the I17/I18 cell semantics, versions read at the tag byte 0, the tag index of validate). (3) cycle: the deterministic BFS spanning forest of rule P8 over the CODEC and HASH edges of the component diagram (rule X6): |E| = 20 (19 CODEC: 4 encoders, 1 loader, 14 decoders; 1 HASH: keccak256), |V| = 17 (Header, BatchHeaderV0, BatchHeaderV1, Bytes, 12 decoder slots, keccak256), kappa = 1, rank = 20 - 17 + 1 = 4. (4) atoms: rule X7 (E1 by position, E2 written and read positions, E6 by the I14 lexicon). (5) laws: rule X8 (P1 per inverse atom, P2 per encoder pair and version, P3-P8 as written, a law over the linked byte carrier scoped to each common version by the tag premise of X8c); statuses by direct evaluation of the layouts and the decoders' conditions (tests_m3/_i24x.py::decide, rule X9); levels and triage by I14's law_evidence over the component atoms. (6) uncovered: what the adopted documents hold outside every component (gaps G1, G2). The build never reads this file; the tests compare holon's outputs with it, and recompute it to check it was not edited.",
